course: dictionary
lesson: 439
title: Archbishop: a very senior church leader
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An archbishop is a very senior bishop. Bishops look after churches, and an archbishop is in charge of the bishops and churches across a large area.
explain: Look at the start of the word. Arch means chief or main, and bishop is a church leader, so archbishop means chief bishop. Use the clue «senior bishop» from the sentence to check: an archbishop is above the other bishops.
explain: «The Church of England is led by bishops, with the Archbishop of Canterbury as senior bishop and the King as Supreme Governor.» Here the words senior bishop tell you the Archbishop of Canterbury is in charge of the other bishops. The capital letters show that Archbishop is a title, and the place name after it tells you which archbishop.
fact: An archbishop is a very senior bishop in charge of bishops and churches in a large area.
fact: The Archbishop of Canterbury is the leading bishop of the Church of England.
fact: Archbishops wear special robes and a tall hat called a mitre.
fact: The Archbishop of Canterbury crowns British kings and queens.
fact: Arch means chief or main, so archbishop means chief bishop.
exercise: «The Church of England is led by bishops, with the Archbishop of Canterbury as senior bishop.» What is an archbishop? | A king who wears a crown | A young child who sings in the church choir | *A very senior bishop in charge of bishops and churches in a large area | A tall hat worn only by ducks
exercise: Who crowns British kings and queens? | *The Archbishop of Canterbury | A bishop from a small village | The Mouse from the story | A church bell ringer
exercise: «When the Mouse says the archbishop found it advisable, the Duck asks, Found what?» What does advisable mean here? | A loud noise | A tall hat | *A sensible idea | A frog or a worm
test: What do archbishops wear on their heads? | *A tall hat called a mitre | A cap with a feather | A helmet | A crown
test: In archbishop, what does arch mean? | *Chief or main | Very cold | Hidden under the ground | Quiet and gentle
exam: Using the clue «senior bishop», what does archbishop mean? | A dog that guards a church | A helper who serves in the king's palace | *A very senior bishop in charge of bishops and churches in a large area | A bishop who has just retired
